  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: 6 original items plus 1 that came in while I worked, all closed.\n\nFrank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: I first renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill. That was based on his last valid potassium, 4.5 on 1/20/26. The 5.9 from 8/27 didn't count because the sample was hemolyzed, so I ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002). Then an outside BMP collected 10/20 arrived with a valid potassium of 5.8. I cancelled the refill before anything was dispensed, created an urgent review task for you (task-t0020, about mr-00283) and sent him a correction. The repeat BMP order is still active.\n\nSamuel Price (pt-0030):\n- Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: the two patient/pharmacy requests and the later pharmacy re-request were treated as one. Renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004): eGFR is 58 (corrected) and his HbA1c of 7.1 from the outside lab on 8/19 is recent enough.\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: I renewed it first, then the lab corrected his 10/6 creatinine to 1.49. That is 35.5% above his level before the dose increase, which the protocol treats like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. I cancelled the refill (not dispensed), created an urgent review task for you (task-t0021, about mr-00295) and sent him a correction.\n\nMarcus Webb (pt-0031):\n- Metformin 500 mg: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). I disregarded the eGFR of 39 from 10/14 because the lab marked it entered in error. His valid eGFR is 90–92.\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: I first sent a 30-day bridge with a BMP order, because his last BMP was more than 12 months old. A valid BMP from 10/22 then arrived (potassium 4.6), so I replaced the bridge with a 90-day supply and 1 refill (mr-t0019) and told him.\n\nPatients were told what was done, and I wrote a chart note for each one. The usual metformin and lisinopril prescriptions they were on were closed out when I placed the refills, and cancelling a refill doesn't reopen them. So Mr. Odum and Mr. Price have no active lisinopril prescription until you review.\n\nStill needs action:\n1. Cancel Mr. Webb's BMP order (sr-t0006). It's no longer needed and I had no way to cancel it.\n2. Results-queue items for these patients (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004) are reviewed and acted on but left open for you to sign off. I didn't touch other patients' results.",
